course: dictionary
lesson: 8706
title: Senators and how they make laws
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A senator is a member of a senate, a group of people who make laws. Read the sentence «Then the general Julius Caesar grew so powerful that senators killed him». The word senators is near words like powerful and killed, so the clues suggest senators were people with real power in Rome.
explain: The clues in a sentence can also tell you which kind of senator is meant. «Every US state has two senators, big or small» tells you that a senator represents a state, and every state gets the same number of senators.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? In «Every US state has two senators», you can swap in lawmakers from a state and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A senator is a member of a senate, a group of people who make laws.
fact: Countries with senators include the USA, Canada, Australia and Ireland.
fact: In ancient Rome, a senator was a member of the Roman Senate.
fact: Every US state has two senators, whether it is big or small.
fact: You can write «Senator Smith» when you give the name of a senator.
exercise: «Every US state has two senators, big or small.» How many senators does each US state have? | *Two | Three | One | Fifty
exercise: In ancient Rome, what was a senator? | A Roman farmer | *A member of the Roman Senate | A Roman emperor | A kind of Roman soldier
exercise: «Then the general Julius Caesar grew so powerful that senators killed him.» Who killed Caesar? | Augustus | *Senators | California | Generals
test: What is a senate? | A kind of horse race | A place where people sell goods | *A group of people who make laws | A type of Roman coin
test: «His adopted son Augustus became the first emperor.» Who became the first emperor after Caesar was killed? | *Augustus | Julius Caesar | A senator from California | Wyoming
exam: «California has more than fifty» House members but «Wyoming has one». Why do they have different numbers? | It has more senators | It is nearer to Rome | *It has more people, so it gets more members in the House | Its people are richer
